{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug Phase 1 RCA — post-release provenance verifier. Problem: `gh attestation verify` returned GitHub API 404 for the published 0.11.0 wheel. Proven root cause: docs/releasing.md and the release AC incorrectly use GitHub Artifact Attestations tooling (default store: GitHub API; default predicate: https://slsa.dev/provenance/v1) to verify the PEP 740 bundle that pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish uploads to PyPI with predicate https://docs.pypi.org/attestations/publish/v1. Proof: run 31155046833/job/92792813274 logged generation/upload of the publish/v1 DSSE for wheel digest 521c8a08a58ae5581ad6cb51ba3a15de45f666615bb9a86ada68836ca16a1daf; PyPI integrity API exposes one bundle; `pypi-attestations verify pypi <wheel> --repository https://github.com/navapbc/rebar` returned OK. GitHub digest lookups under both SLSA and PyPI predicates returned 404, and the 0.10.1 wheel control fails identically, rejecting propagation and malformed-publication hypotheses. Classification: documentation/acceptance-contract defect, not a defective 0.11.0 artifact. The release criterion will use the authoritative PyPI verifier; the runbook/workflow-comment correction is follow-up work."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786085632559813001,"uuid":"84f76c6f-15f8-4064-a450-8ab20ddc5add"}